#Problem APEX 5.1.32

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Integrals)
## DBsection(Antiderivatives (without trigonometric functions))
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## KEYWORDS(indefinite integral, 'initial value problem')
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('5.1')
## Problem1('32')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric')->flags->set(tolerance => 0.01, tolType => "absolute");

$a = random( 2, 9);
$x = random( 1, 4);
$y = random(-5, 5);

$f = "$a^x";

$C     = $y - ($a**$x) / (ln($a));
$f_int = Formula("$a^x/ln($a) + $C")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML
Find the function [`f(x)`] described by the given initial value problem.

[```  f'(x) = [$f], \quad f([$x]) = [$y].```]

[`f(x) =`] [____]{$f_int}{30}.
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
[`
 f(x)= \int [$f] \, dx = \dfrac{[$a]^x}{\ln [$a]} + C.  `]  Find [`C`] by setting [`f([$x]) = [$y].`]
END_PGML_HINT

$C = int($C * 10**4) / 10**4;
BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

[```
 f(x)= \int [$f] \, dx = \dfrac{[$a]^x}{\ln [$a]} + C.  ```]

Find [`C`] by setting [`f([$x]) = [$y].`]

[```
  \begin{aligned}  
     \dfrac{[$a]^{[$x]}}{\ln [$a]} + C &= [$y] \\
     C &=[$y] - \dfrac{[$a]^{[$x]}}{\ln [$a]} \approx [$C].
  \end{aligned}
```]

Thus, [``f(x) = \dfrac{[$a]^x}{\ln [$a]} + [$C]``].

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
